{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.ConfinementLevel"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gb_spectral_sequence_e2_iso","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gb_spectral_sequence_e2_iso","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L100-L108","doc":"**E_2 collapse theorem.** Under the E_2 collapse extension,\nthe convergence map is bijective at every filtration level —\ni.e., the spectral sequence's $E_2$ page IS the $E_\\infty$ page\nup to the iso. This is the formal statement of \"no free\nparameters beyond E_2\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequenceCollapsesAtE2.convergeTo_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequenceCollapsesAtE2.convergeTo_injective","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L98-L98","doc":"The convergence map is injective (combined with surjectivity\nfrom the parent class, this gives iso at E_2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequenceCollapsesAtE2.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequenceCollapsesAtE2.mk","kind":"ctor","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequenceCollapsesAtE2.toGBSpectralSequence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequenceCollapsesAtE2.toGBSpectralSequence","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L94-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequenceCollapsesAtE2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequenceCollapsesAtE2","kind":"class","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L80-L98","doc":"**T4 scaffold: E_2 spectral-sequence collapse extension class.**\n\nPer `prop:spectral-sequence-collapse` and the audit\n`docs/audits/2026-05-24-derivation-chain-gb-jet-orders-and-pentagon.md`\n§2 (Step 7 — GB filtration / spectral sequence): the GB\nspectral sequence collapses at $E_2$ because Pentagon\ncoherence forces the higher differentials $d_k$ for $k \\geq 2$\nto vanish.\n\nExtends `GBSpectralSequence` with the explicit collapse-at-E_2\ncondition: the convergence map is iso (not just surjective) at\nevery filtration level. Under this strengthening, every higher\njet $h^{2k}$ for $k \\geq 2$ is *determined* by the $E_2$ data\n(the $\\ell = 0, 1, 2$ pieces). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.gb_spectral_sequence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.gb_spectral_sequence","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L68-L78","doc":"**GB spectral sequence proposition.**\n\nConditional on `[GBSpectralSequence R]`, the differential\nsquares to zero and the spectral sequence converges. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:gb-spectral-sequence","label":"prop:gb-spectral-sequence","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/gb-spectral-sequence.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.e_infty_converges","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.e_infty_converges","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L64-L64","doc":"Convergence: the spectral sequence stabilises onto `E_∞`.\nCf. gemini-code-assist review on PR #535. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.convergeTo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.convergeTo","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L61-L61","doc":"Convergence map `J^ℓ / J^{ℓ+1} → E_∞^ℓ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.E_infty_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.E_infty_add","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.E_infty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.E_infty","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Convergence target: at each level ℓ the `E_∞` page identifies\nwith the associated graded.  The class records the target type\nand the convergence map, and asserts that the latter is\nsurjective. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.d_squared_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.d_squared_zero","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The differential squares to zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.differential","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.differential","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The differential `d : J^ℓ / J^{ℓ+1} → J^ℓ / J^{ℓ+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.gradedAdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.gradedAdd","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Each graded piece is an additive group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.graded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.graded","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The associated-graded piece at filtration level `ℓ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence.mk","kind":"ctor","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.GBSpectralSequence","kind":"class","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/GBSpectralSequence.lean#L28-L64","doc":"**GB spectral sequence on the GS-filtered Hecke algebra.**\n\nA class instance carries:\n* `filtration : ℕ → Type*` — the filtered pieces `J^ℓ(q)` (or,\n  strictly, the associated graded `J^ℓ / J^{ℓ+1}` at level ℓ).\n* `differential : ∀ ℓ, filtration ℓ → filtration ℓ` — the\n  direct sum `d = d_H + d_F + d_{YB}` of the three GS rewriting\n  rules, lifted to the Hochschild cochain complex.\n* `d_squared_zero` — the differential squares to zero\n  (Cartan–Eilenberg).\n* `e_infty_converges` — the spectral sequence converges to the\n  associated graded of the Hecke algebra.\n\nEach field encodes a substantial mathematical statement; the\nclass is the conditional-class wrapper for the proposition\n`prop:gb-spectral-sequence`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}